The Security Council,

Recalling its previous relevant resolutions on the situation between Iraq and Kuwait, in particular resolutions 687 (1991), 833 (1993), 1284 (1999), 2107 (2013), and 2621 (2022),

Reaffirming its commitment to the sovereignty, territorial integrity, and political independence of both Iraq and Kuwait, and to the principles of the Charter of the United Nations,

Welcoming the steady improvement in bilateral relations between the Government of Iraq and the Government of Kuwait, and commending the constructive engagement, high-level visits, and ongoing dialogue between both Governments aimed at resolving all outstanding bilateral issues,

Expressing appreciation for the continued commitment of the Government of Iraq to fulfilling its remaining international obligations under relevant Security Council resolutions, particularly resolution 2107 (2013),

Acknowledging with appreciation the crucial humanitarian role played by the International Committee of the Red Cross (ICRC) in chairing the Tripartite Commission and its Technical Sub-Committee, and commending the steadfast commitment of the members of the Tripartite Commission, including Kuwait, Saudi Arabia, the United States, the United Kingdom, and France, alongside the United Nations Assistance Mission for Iraq (UNAMI) as an observer,

Welcoming the ongoing efforts to locate and identify the remains of missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals, including the identification and repatriation of human remains over recent years through DNA analysis and forensic collaboration, but expressing concern that a significant number of missing persons remain unaccounted for more than three decades after the events,

Recognizing the profound humanitarian imperative of providing answers to the families of the missing persons without further delay,

Noting with regret the lack of substantial progress in recent years in locating the Kuwaiti National Archives, and emphasizing the importance of returning all missing Kuwaiti property, including the national archives and military equipment,

Taking note of the pending transition and planned drawdown of UNAMI pursuant to resolution 2732 (2024), and underscoring the vital need to maintain an effective, sustained, and dedicated United Nations follow-up mechanism to support and oversee the resolution of these outstanding humanitarian files,

Stressing the importance of adhering to international law, the Charter of the United Nations, and relevant Security Council resolutions regarding the maintenance of international peace and security, including the inviolability of the international boundary between Iraq and Kuwait as demarcated by the United Nations Iraq-Kuwait Boundary Demarcation Commission and guaranteed by the Security Council in resolution 833 (1993),

1. Calls upon the Government of Iraq to continue its diligent cooperation with the Government of Kuwait, the Tripartite Commission, and the ICRC to advance the search for missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals, and to accelerate efforts to locate, excavate, and identify remains at potential burial sites;

2. Urges the Government of Iraq to intensify its search for the missing Kuwaiti National Archives and other Kuwaiti property, to pursue new and innovative investigative leads, and to ensure the swift return of any located property to the Government of Kuwait;

3. Commends the Government of Kuwait for its unwavering cooperation, humanitarian approach, and logistical support provided to the Tripartite Commission and the Iraqi authorities in their joint efforts;

4. Encourages both Iraq and Kuwait to continue their constructive bilateral dialogue to resolve all remaining issues in a spirit of good neighbourliness, including through the Joint Committee on Demarcation of Maritime Boundaries beyond Boundary Pillar 162, in accordance with the United Nations Convention on the Law of the Sea and international law, and reaffirms the importance of full respect for the sovereignty and territorial integrity of both States and resolution 833 (1993);

5. Decides to establish a dedicated United Nations mechanism, under the direct authority of the Secretary-General, upon the conclusion of UNAMI’s mandate, to continue facilitating, coordinating, and reporting on efforts to resolve the issues of missing Kuwaiti and third-country nationals and the return of Kuwaiti property, including the National Archives;

6. Requests the Secretary-General to appoint a High-Level Coordinator, with appropriate expertise and administrative support, to oversee these efforts in close consultation with the Governments of Iraq and Kuwait, the Tripartite Commission, and the ICRC;

7. Further requests the Secretary-General to report to the Security Council every six months on progress made in the implementation of all matters covered by this resolution, including the activities of the High-Level Coordinator and the Tripartite mechanism;

8. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

